{"name":"Starfleet Blue","hex":"#0096ff","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"starfleet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fleet of starships; a space navy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/starfleet"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Star Trek","blocks":[{"text":"Star Trek is an American science fiction media franchise created by Gene Roddenberry and owned by Paramount, which began with the series of the same name and became a worldwide pop culture phenomenon. Since its creation, the franchise has expanded into various films, television series, video games, novels, and comic books, and it has become one of the most recognizable and highest-grossing media franchises of all time."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Emblem.svg/330px-Emblem.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Trek"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Gene_roddenberry_1976.jpg/330px-Gene_roddenberry_1976.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Gene_roddenberry_1976.jpg/330px-Gene_roddenberry_1976.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Star Trek creator, producer and writer Gene Roddenberry (c. 1976)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGene_roddenberry_1976.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Leonard_Nimoy_William_Shatner_Star_Trek_1968.JPG/500px-Leonard_Nimoy_William_Shatner_Star_Trek_1968.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Leonard_Nimoy_William_Shatner_Star_Trek_1968.JPG/1280px-Leonard_Nimoy_William_Shatner_Star_Trek_1968.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Leonard_Nimoy_William_Shatner_Star_Trek_1968.JPG/500px-Leonard_Nimoy_William_Shatner_Star_Trek_1968.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeonard_Nimoy_William_Shatner_Star_Trek_1968.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/QTXP_20121019_Destination_Star_Trek_London_MG_2284.jpg/500px-QTXP_20121019_Destination_Star_Trek_London_MG_2284.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Q